  #line-at(58.944pt, 306.05pt, "Abstract")
  #line-at(90.024pt, 306.05pt, "— ")
  #line-at(110.78pt, 306.05pt, "Backside ")
  #line-at(156.95pt, 306.05pt, "power‑delivery‑network ")
  #line-at(261.53pt, 306.05pt, "(BSPDN) ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 316.37pt, "schemes require wafer‑to‑wafer bonding steps that do not leave ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 326.69pt, "high order shape changes or localized stresses in the bonded stack ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 337.13pt, "to ensure that these don’t get transferred to the thinned wafer for ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 347.45pt, "further lithographic exposure. However, bonding mechanics ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 357.77pt, "involve strong adhesive forces which can inherently create ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 368.09pt, "localized distortions that lithography tools must eventually ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 378.53pt, "compensate. Some contributors to grid distortion of the target ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 388.85pt, "wafer are, method of bond initiation, bond front velocity ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 399.17pt, "variations, and lack of symmetry between the wafers. In this work, ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 409.49pt, "we evaluate a low‑distortion bonding approach in the SUSS XBA ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 419.95pt, "tool, where some of these contributors are tackled at the source, ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 430.27pt, "namely by initiating the bond without a localized external force, ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 440.59pt, "and keeping the wafers compliant & symmetric during bonding. ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 450.91pt, "Wafers are bonded with a slight pre-stress due to controlled gas ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 461.35pt, "pressure applied over the whole backside of the wafers throughout ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 471.67pt, "bonding. Wafer‑shape measurements of the bonded stacks are ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 481.99pt, "used to perform gradient‑based in-plane-displacements (IPD) ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 492.31pt, "modelling to estimate bonding‑induced grid distortion. We ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 502.63pt, "identify a persistent ring‑shaped distortion region on the wafer - ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 513.07pt, "whose origin we suspect to originate from bonding mechanics itself ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 523.39pt, "– the bondwave’s interruption. Dense scanner metrology is used ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 533.71pt, "on patterned-bonded wafers to confirm the location and severity ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 544.03pt, "of distortion predictions from patterned wafer geometry (PWG) ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 554.47pt, "measurements. On the PWG distortion maps and scanner grid ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 564.79pt, "readouts, we perform alignment and CPE modelling with different ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 575.11pt, "field layouts. Sub‑10 nm levels of residual grid distortion are ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 585.46pt, "achievable with relatively low-order correction models, and ≤ 3 ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 595.9pt, "nm by using advanced CPE models. These results demonstrate ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 606.22pt, "that pneumatically warped bonding yields low‑distortion bonded ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 616.54pt, "stacks, and that simple process tuning can decouple the dominant ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 626.98pt, "distortion source from edge‑related variability.")
  #line-at(58.944pt, 647.26pt, "Keywords— bonding induced distortion, wafer bonding, fusion ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 657.7pt, "bonding, direct bonding, back side lithography, BS-PDN ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(132.38pt, 678.94pt, "I.")
  #line-at(146.06pt, 678.94pt, "I")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(149.42pt, 678.94pt, "NTRODUCTION")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(59.784pt, 693.936pt, "Wafer‑to‑wafer bonding is becoming an essential building ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 704.856pt, "block for advanced logic integration, particularly in schemes ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 715.776pt, "that rely on post‑bond thinning and backside patterning [1,2]. ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 306.53pt, "One of the most promising pathways extending the logic ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 317.45pt, "roadmap is the backside power‑delivery‑network (BSPDN) ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 328.37pt, "concept at the standard‑cell level, where a lithography step is ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 339.29pt, "performed on the thinned backside of a bonded pair. This ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 350.21pt, "application requires stringent overlay requirements between ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 361.13pt, "features defined before and after bonding [3]. ")
  #line-at(329.47pt, 378.05pt, "Meeting these alignment targets is complicated by the fact ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 388.97pt, "that wafer bonding inherently modifies wafer geometry, creating ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 399.89pt, "a fundamental bottleneck for BSPDN implementation. The act ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 410.81pt, "of pressing two wafers into contact—together with their ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 421.75pt, "pre-existing shapes, stress states, and bonding dynamics—")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 432.67pt, "introduces distortions that persist in the stack and alter the ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 443.59pt, "lithography target map [4]. While scanners can correct ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 454.51pt, "low-order components of the resulting grid deformation, the ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 465.43pt, "higher-order components require dense metrology to quantify ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 476.35pt, "and are therefore more difficult to anticipate or compensate. ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 487.27pt, "These higher‑order components arise from several physical ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 498.19pt, "contributors, including the method of bond initiation, variations ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 509.11pt, "in bond‑front velocity, hardware imprints, or any other localized ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 520.15pt, "stress residues in the bonded stack which can even arise from ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 531.07pt, "bonder-chuck contamination. ")
  #line-at(329.47pt, 547.99pt, "Given the growing relevance of backside patterning and the ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 558.91pt, "need for predictable overlay behavior after thinning, ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 569.83pt, "understanding how bonding mechanics shape the distortion map ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 580.75pt, "is essential. In particular, bonding configurations that minimize ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 591.7pt, "high-order shape changes are of interest for enabling ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 602.62pt, "reproducible, low‑distortion bonded stacks which would shift ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 613.54pt, "distribution of backside (BS) print overlay content to lower ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 624.46pt, "orders of the correction content, which could minimize the use ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 635.38pt, "of dense metrology on the BS. ")
  #line-at(329.47pt, 652.3pt, "In this work, we investigate such a bonding approach and ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 663.22pt, "evaluate ")
  #line-at(359.332pt, 663.22pt, "its ")
  #line-at(379.969pt, 663.22pt, "impact ")
  #line-at(418.106pt, 663.22pt, "on ")
  #line-at(439.341pt, 663.22pt, "wafer‑scale ")
  #line-at(496.093pt, 663.22pt, "distortion ")
  #line-at(545.266pt, 663.22pt, "using ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 674.14pt, "complementary metrology techniques. To quantify distortion, ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 685.06pt, "we combine: ")
  #line-at(333.07pt, 702.456pt, "1.")
  #line-at(351.07pt, 702.456pt, "double‑thickness wafer‑shape characterization using ")
  #line-at(351.07pt, 713.976pt, "PWG interferometry, followed by gradient‑based (1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(562.68pt, 710.496pt, "st")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#ffffff"))
