  #line-at(59.784pt, 136.22pt, "The paper characterizes the resulting distortion signatures, ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 147.14pt, "identifies the physical origins of localized deformation, and ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 158.06pt, "examines the extent to which scanner alignment and correction ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 168.98pt, "models can compensate these effects in the context of ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 179.9pt, "BSPDN‑type applications. We apply standard 6‑parameter ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 190.82pt, "wafer‑alignment models to separate low‑order distortion ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 201.74pt, "components from the residuals. Most distortion introduced ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 212.66pt, "during bonding appears as low‑order terms, which scanners can ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 223.58pt, "readily calibrate and correct. The remaining higher‑order ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 234.5pt, "distortion is symmetrically distributed (over the wafer scale) but ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 245.42pt, "localized at some radial locations. These localized regions can ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 256.37pt, "be further reduced using scanner correction‑per‑exposure (CPE) ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 267.29pt, "models. Different field layouts have been used to indicate the ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 278.21pt, "suitability of this bonding technique for, for example use ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 289.13pt, "advanced packaging lithography, or advanced lithography in ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 300.05pt, "immersion or EUV scanner field layouts for advanced logic ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 310.97pt, "nodes. ")
