  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(274.75pt, 651.94pt, "’, few ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 662.98pt, "millibars) is applied from the center of the chucks towards the ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 673.9pt, "wafer backside such that they bulge outwards away from the ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 684.82pt, "chuck, as shown Fig 1. A higher pressure results in a higher warp ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 695.736pt, "at the center, which can help ensure that the first contact between ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 706.656pt, "the wafers happens at the center (assuming no lack of symmetry ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 717.576pt, "from the stresses in the wafers and the chucks’ hold on the ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 62.88pt, "wafers). The magnitude of contact pressure applied also ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 73.8pt, "determines how compliant the wafers remain during bonding – ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 84.74pt, "resulting in the bond front’s propagation resembling the ideal ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 95.66pt, "case of free-hanging wafers. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#44546a"))
  #line-at(315.07pt, 182.06pt, "Fig. 1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#44546a"))
  #line-at(337.03pt, 182.06pt, " Schematic of the bonding sequence once wafers prepared with ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 192.38pt, "the appropriate surface treatments are chucked in the bond chamber. ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 202.7pt, "Wafers are bulged towards each other by a small gas pressure coming ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 213.14pt, "from the backside. The chucks move towards each other to initiate the ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 223.58pt, "bond. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(315.07pt, 244.22pt, "The bond is initiated by moving the chucks towards each other ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 255.17pt, "with a prescribed velocity (10s of µm/s). Since the work of ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 266.09pt, "adhesion of these atomically smooth surfaces prepared with ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 277.01pt, "CMP, plasma activation and water rinse is very high")
  #line-at(523.56pt, 277.01pt, "(~0.1 J/m")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(561.12pt, 273.53pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(564.24pt, 277.01pt, ",")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 288.05pt, "[5]), the wafers instantly adhere and a bond front spontaneously ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 298.97pt, "propagates as far as the chucking conditions allow. The chucks ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 309.89pt, "can be programmed to stop moving towards each other such that ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 320.81pt, "the wafers are not compressed together over their whole surface. ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 331.73pt, "This is implemented in XBA’s control software by ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 342.77pt, "programming the ‘")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(392.5pt, 342.77pt, "final gap’")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(432.7pt, 342.77pt, " (henceforth called parameter ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(556.32pt, 342.77pt, "𝐺")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(563.52pt, 342.77pt, ") ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 353.81pt, "between the unbonded parts of the wafer (close to the edge) ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 364.73pt, "which the bond chamber is allowed to reach – typically up to ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 375.65pt, "100 ")
