  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(59.784pt, 694.296pt, "The stack in the patterned wafers is constructed by ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 705.216pt, "sequentially depositing dielectric layers on a silicon substrate. ")
  #line-at(45.36pt, 716.136pt, "The stack consists of Cu alignment and overlay markers made ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 62.88pt, "using copper damascene method, etched in 150 nm deep SiO₂ ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 73.8pt, "layer, and finished with plating, CMP, and further depositions ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 84.74pt, "including 30 nm thick SiCN layers, 250 nm SiO₂ and finally ~25 ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 95.66pt, "nm thick SiCN as the bonding interface. Both the device and ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 106.58pt, "carrier wafers are made with the similar stack, except for the ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 117.5pt, "patterns etched into each pair to make the markers (which are ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 128.42pt, "complementary pairs). ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(315.07pt, 145.82pt, "A.")
  #line-at(329.47pt, 145.82pt, "Enabling dense scanner metrology ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(315.07pt, 159.86pt, "The bonding of patterned wafer pairs is done using the same ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 170.78pt, "hydrophilic bonding sequence as discussed above in sections II ")
  #line-at(315.07pt, 181.7pt, "and III. A schematic in Fig 5 shows very briefly the flow of using ")
